                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Surgical Nursing is an applied discipline guided by theories from social sciences and natural sciences, aimed at serving human health. It is an important part of nursing, primarily focusing on the basic theories, fundamental knowledge, and essential skills of surgical nursing, as well as the overall care of patients with common and frequently occurring diseases in various surgical specialties. It is a core clinical course for nursing students.<br><br>This course is divided into three parts. The General Part focuses on introducing the course, surgical shock, nutritional support, organ transplantation, surgical infections, burns, operating room procedures, anesthesia, and care of surgical patients. The General and Specialized Surgery Part emphasizes the clinical characteristics and management of common and frequently occurring diseases in various surgical departments.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
